body:

<div id="page-body-countdown-container"></div>

<img src="/current/starship-pad-boat.jpg" alt="Photo of the SpaceX Starship on the pad, with a boat in the foreground" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; margin-top: 5px; margin-bottom: 20px;">

Join Star Fleet for the first-ever flight attempt of a fully-reusable orbital rocket, the "holy grail" of rocketry, and the first ever landing attempt of both the Starship upper stage and the V3 version of the Super Heavy booster!
We're running a separate trip at a discount to view the landing, from an close-up spot.

For ship landing, we plan to be in the mouth of the Brownsville ship channel, with is both nearly as close as possible to the pad while having an ideal view of the Starship on approach as it makes a wide 270 degree turn with our location essentially at the pivot point.


**LATEST LANDING UPDATE**:
As of *Friday November 14* at 11 am CST, SpaceX remains GO for catch today around 3:20 PM CST, and vehicle and weather are both looking good!
As such, we've opened up another boat, the Osprey, which we had a great time on yesterday, so go ahead and book your spots now.
Looking forward to seeing you all there!

*We have **[a Whats App community](INSERT_URL_1) that we highly recommend you join**, with channels for announcements, insider launch updates, discussion, questions and more!
We also use it for early tickets, special community events and more!
You can also follow our [Twitter](https://twitter.com/StarFleetTours), [Instagram](https://instagram.com/starfleettours/) and [Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/starfleettours/) for announcements and updates.
Thanks!*

